meta {
  name: Get Pay Statement
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/payouts/statements/{{payoutsStatementId}}
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{payoutsOwnerToken}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // Nobody was on the structure (the demo producer was already on another).
  if (!bru.getVar("payoutsStatementId")) bru.runner.skipRequest();
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("carries the Commission Statement's sections", function () {
    const s = res.getBody();
    expect(s).to.include.keys(
      "structure", "premiumLines", "deals", "chargebacks", "bonuses",
      "indicators", "adjustments", "totals", "warnings", "allstateBindId"
    );
    expect(s.status).to.equal("draft");
  });

  test("its lines add up to its totals", function () {
    const s = res.getBody();
    const cents = function (n) { return Math.round(n * 100); };
    const gross = s.premiumLines.reduce(function (sum, l) { return sum + cents(l.grossPremium); }, 0);
    const net = s.premiumLines.reduce(function (sum, l) { return sum + cents(l.netCommission); }, 0);
    expect(gross).to.equal(cents(s.totals.grossPremium));
    // Commission is the rate on net premium (10 Nov 2026); only a statement
    // calculated before carries chargebackImpact.
    expect(net).to.equal(cents(s.totals.grossCommission) - cents(s.totals.chargebackImpact || 0));
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /payouts/statements/:id — one statement (PAC-178)

  **Module** — `payouts`. **Permission** — `payouts:read`, under the same
  rule as **List Pay Statements**: your own once sent, or anything your scope
  reaches with `payouts:write`. Anything else is a `404` — never a `403`, so
  whether a statement exists is not given away.

  **Response `200`** — the summary fields plus:
  | field | |
  |---|---|
  | allstateBindId | the "SOK number", the statement's Producer ID |
  | timeZone | the agency's zone the month was cut in |
  | structure | the payment structure as it was when computed (rates, lead-source rates named, hat trick, tiers, `tiersStackable`, `teamBonusEligible`) |
  | premiumLines[] | the carrier production table: `{ carrier, leadSourceId, leadSourceName, appointed, grossPremium, chargebacks, netPremium, ratePercent, rateSource, grossCommission, netCommission, bundleRate, minBundleRatePercent, bundleShortfall }`. Commission is the rate on **net premium** (sold less charged back), so `grossCommission` = `netCommission`; a statement calculated before 10 Nov 2026 also has `chargebackImpact`, deducted from its commission on sold premium. A sale paid a **lead-source rate** is on a line of its own ("Allstate · JYA leads"); every other sale on a carrier is on the carrier's line. Every appointed carrier is listed, sold or not. `rateSource` is `carrier`, `any`, `lead_source_carrier`, `lead_source` or `none` (no rule covers it — paid 0%, with a warning). |
  | deals[] | the month's sales: `{ dealId, soldDate, soldDay, clientName, policyTypes, carriers, policyCount, premium, leadSourceId, leadSourceName, isBundle, householdId }` (a bundle = 2+ policies; `householdId` absent on statements stored before 10 Nov 2026) |
  | chargebacks[] | `{ chargebackId, policyId, householdId, policyNumber, policyType, carrier, customerName, amount, occurredAt, occurredDay, reason, source, leadSourceId, ratePercent, excluded, excludedNote }` — each taken off the premium of the line of the sale it reverses (`commissionDeduction` only on statements calculated before 10 Nov 2026) |
  | bonuses | `hatTrick { enabled, dealsPerDay, bonusAmount, days[], amount }`, `individual { stackable, reached[], amount }`, `team { eligible, met, poolAmount, pool, groupPool, groupPremium, amount }`, `salespersonOfMonth { enabled, winner, amount }` |
  | indicators | `{ tier: { level, thresholdPremium } \| null, bundleRate, hatTricks, somStatus: winner\|none\|off, complianceStatus: compliant\|non_compliant, failedAudits }` |
  | adjustments[] | the manager's corrections: the entered SPIFFs, compliance adjustment and other adjustments (**Update Pay Statement Adjustments**), and left-out chargebacks (PAC-182) |
  | warnings[] | e.g. "Allstate bundle rate 71% is below the 83% minimum." — a flag; pay is not changed |

  `totals.netCommission` = commission (the rate on net premium) + tier + team
  + Salesperson of the Month + hat trick + SPIFFs + compliance adjustment +
  other adjustments (the two adjustments are negative). A chargeback comes off
  the premium once; its commission is not deducted again (owner, 10 Nov 2026). Sold premium is gross (the Owner dashboard's figure);
  `Deal.chargebackAdjustment` is not applied — the ledger row carries it.

  Skipped when the run had no statement to read.

  ## The 2026 comp-plan fields

  - `inputs` — the figures the manager entered (**Update Pay Statement
    Inputs**), each `null` when not; `inputsNeeded` — which of them the
    structure reads.
  - `totals` gains `basePay`, `stipend`, `rateStepBonus`,
    `overrideCommission`, `agencyBonus`, `producerOfYearBonus`,
    `complianceReduction` (≤ 0), `referralAdjustment` (±) and `netPay`
    (base pay + stipend + net commission). Absent on statements computed
    before them: read them as 0, and net pay as net commission.
  - `premiumLines[].rateStep` — the step a stepped rate was paid at.
  - `bonuses` gains `rateSteps`, `agency`, `overrides`, `referrals`,
    `producerOfYear`, `teamBlocked` and `compliance`.
}
